  "body": "## What is this?\n\nThis PR adds the `SpellCheckCustomDictionary` API, exposing `window.spellCheckDictionary` in secure contexts. It allows pages to add or remove words from a per-document custom spelling exemption list, so those words are not flagged as misspelled by the UA's spell checker.\n\nThis accompanies a [W3C TAG review](https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/) and prototype implementations in Chromium and WebKit.\n\n## What changed?\n\n- Defines a new **`concept-custom-spelling-exemptions`** ordered set on each `Document`, initially empty, matched ASCII case-insensitively\n- Adds an integration hook: if a word matches the exemption list, the UA should not indicate a spelling error for it\n- Defines the **`SpellCheckCustomDictionary`** interface with `addWords(sequence<DOMString>)` and `removeWords(sequence<DOMString>)` methods\n- Exposes `window.spellCheckDictionary` as a `[SecureContext, SameObject]` readonly attribute on `Window`\n- Adds a conformance requirement that **UAs not supporting spell checking must not expose the attribute**, preserving `if (window.spellCheckDictionary)` as a reliable feature-detection pattern\n\n## Notes for reviewers\n\n- The exemption list is intentionally not persisted, not shared across documents/frames/browsing contexts, and is discarded when the `Document` is destroyed\n- The `has()` method (checking whether a word is in the list) is deliberately not exposed to JS — there is no need to expose dictionary contents to the page\n- Names (`spellCheckDictionary`, `addWords`, `removeWords`) are expected bikeshed candidates\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12376/index.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 15, 2026, 7:56 PM UTC (fd5b5b1)\">/index.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12376/7fe76d0...fd5b5b1/index.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 15, 2026, 7:56 PM UTC (fd5b5b1)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12376/interaction.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 15, 2026, 7:56 PM UTC (fd5b5b1)\">/interaction.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12376/7fe76d0...fd5b5b1/interaction.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 15, 2026, 7:56 PM UTC (fd5b5b1)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12376/nav-history-apis.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 15, 2026, 7:56 PM UTC (fd5b5b1)\">/nav-history-apis.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12376/7fe76d0...fd5b5b1/nav-history-apis.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 15, 2026, 7:56 PM UTC (fd5b5b1)\">diff</a> )",
